# candor effect policy for pgman.
#
# DATA-ACCESS BOUNDARY: direct database access (the `Db` effect — a query/exec/transaction call) must
# stay in the DATA LAYER:
#   - src/conn.rs   — the connection + transaction primitives
#   - src/query/    — the query modules (lint, explain, schema, …)
#
# A UI/app function that reaches the database DIRECTLY is an architectural leak: it should route through
# the data layer instead, so connection handling, transactions, and query construction stay in one place.
# (Transitively reaching Db via a conn/query call is fine — only a DIRECT Db call outside the data layer
# is a violation.)
#
# Enforced in CI by ci/candor-check.sh using the stable scanner (`cargo install candor-scan`) — no
# nightly toolchain. The nightly candor lint's `cargo candor policy` expresses the same intent as
# `deny Db` scoped to the app layer (AS-EFF-006).
#
# Known exception (documented in ci/candor-check.sh): `app::run_cost_explain` — a self-contained
# EXPLAIN-cost helper still living in app.rs. Its natural home is src/query/explain.rs; moving it there
# drops the exception and tightens the boundary.

deny Db   # outside the data layer (src/conn.rs, src/query/) — see ci/candor-check.sh for the scoped check
